Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: GGML_ARIFI_IQ4XS_MMVQ default back to legacy on every
 vendor - the 6-cell route failed the greedy identity gate

Pre-registered R48b-class ship rule: token-identical greedy text 3 prompts x 2 files. The flip binary (b1bab0ac1) gave 9/12 identical and 3/12 DIFFER, all on the Unsloth Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL file (b6-p1, b6-p2, b4-p2), even though timing (6 cells >=5/6, >=1.03) and PPL at b=6/4/3/2 passed. route stays opt-in with the same 6-cell admit. Un-flip proof: startup legacy (default), targeted 101/101 with 0 iq4_xs MMVQ decisions, greedy b6-f2-p1/p2 default == legacy; =route 101/101, MMVQ at exactly the 6 cells. Registry row updated.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-262 R75 iq4_xs MMVQ route, Opus 5 kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: none by default (legacy); route opt-in is op-level only, served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-262
Receipts: r75-evidence/56-greedy-verdict.txt, r75-evidence/60-unflip-log.txt
