`, `13-paired-ffn2.txt`), `default/route` median [min..max] wins/6: `n=5` **1.067** [1.032..1.104] 6/6, `n=6` **1.109** 6/6, `n=7` **1.095** 6/6, `n=8` **1.204** [1.185..1.266] 6/6; `n=1` 0.999 (untouched). `marg(4..8)` falls **113.8 → 5.4 us/col** against q4_K's 27 — the lane's ship criterion. Re-taken on the shipped `n>=5` binary: `n=5..8` = 1.056/1.120/1.075/1.152, 5-6/6. **The `k` gate is measured, not copied**: at 5120x17408 (`k=17408`) forced MMVQ **LOSES**, unanimously at `n=5` (0.962 [0.921..0.997], **0/6** rounds won) and near-unanimously at `n=6` (0.968, 1/6); at `n=7`/`n=8` the medians are 0.988/0.976 but the rounds split 3/6 and 2/6 and the ranges straddle 1.0, so those two are **not** established against the null band and are not claimed (`13-paired-down-head.txt`). The gate ships on the firm end, and its error direction is to NARROW the admit. On the served Q4_K_XL file **90.5% of Q5_K bytes sit at `k<=8192`** (`11-typemix.txt`), so the gate keeps nearly all of the type. **The `n<5` end is NOT established as a loss**: the shipped binary makes `route` at `n=1..4` the identical code path to `default`, and it still read 0.942 at `n=4` — a three-arm null control (`14-null-table.txt`, all legacy, same slots) bounds the slot artifact at only 1-3%, so `n=4` on this shape is **noise-dominated and the lane's least-resolved cell**. `n>=5` is the conservative bound, not a fitted one: it is where `rm_int_n()` gives the MMVQ pipeline 4 rows per workgroup instead of 1. Correctness `test -o MUL_MAT -p type_a=q5_K/q6_K` **152 cases (q5_K 85/85 + q6_K 67/67), 0 FAIL, all three arms** (`20-correct-*`), full `MUL_MAT` sweep **2130/2130, 0 FAIL both arms** (`21-mulmat-full-*`), planted RED in `mul_mat_vecq.comp` under `DATA_A_Q5_K && NUM_COLS>1` gives **52/85 = 33 FAIL cases with `route`, every one at `n=5..8`, and 85/85 with `legacy`**, restored byte-identical (`40-restore-proof.txt`). 27B text: **6/6 token-identical**, 3 greedy prompts x 2 Q4_K_XL files — but that is an